So, what is research? Actually, if you Google the internet, there are so many different definitions of the research

00:23:18.000 --> 00:23:26.000
So in essence, research is considered as systematic and methodical process of inquiry

00:23:26.000 --> 00:23:35.000
Aim at exploring, analyzing, and interpreting information to answer specific questions or solve problems.

00:23:35.000 --> 00:23:43.000
So by establishing research methodologies, researchers can collect reliable data

00:23:43.000 --> 00:23:56.000
draw meaningful conclusions and contribute to the existing body of knowledge. So in essence, research definition emphasize structured inquiry

00:23:56.000 --> 00:24:03.000
Objectivity and evidence-based reasoning and understanding

00:24:03.000 --> 00:24:18.000
So, this just shows one of so many different types of research definition. So in this case, in this definition, research is considered as a careful, systematic and objective investigation

00:24:18.000 --> 00:24:34.000
conducted to obtain valid facts, draw conclusions, and establish principles regarding an identifiable problem in some field of knowledge. Okay.

00:24:34.000 --> 00:24:49.000
Then there are many characteristics of research. I think this slide and the next slide simply just discuss some key characteristics of research. The fourth one is called systematic approach

00:24:49.000 --> 00:25:00.000
So that means that research must follow organized steps to ensure logic data collection, analysis, and interpretation

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:14.000
Then the next one is objective and unbiased. So means that all the conclusions drawn by a research must be based on the evidence rather than the personal opinions

00:25:14.000 --> 00:25:21.000
Or preferences. So research conclusion must be objective, not subjective

00:25:21.000 --> 00:25:32.000
The next one is empirical evidence means that the research findings must be based on the observation, experiments

00:25:32.000 --> 00:25:37.000
or survey. So those the objective data

00:25:37.000 --> 00:25:42.000
That formed the findings of the research.

00:25:42.000 --> 00:25:50.000
Then the clear research question. So this is very important. So every research must have very clear

00:25:50.000 --> 00:26:05.000
research question. Based on this research question, we may have clear research objective and then we also can formulate or consider appropriate research methodology

00:26:05.000 --> 00:26:14.000
So that the outcome of this research can meet the research goal or objective

00:26:14.000 --> 00:26:18.000
Then the next one is replicability.

00:26:18.000 --> 00:26:33.000
So replicability means that other researchers should be able to reproduce the study and achieve similar results. For example, if we designed a credit card fraud detection method

00:26:33.000 --> 00:26:36.000
For Bank A

00:26:36.000 --> 00:26:42.000
that produce very good result, then the same method should

00:26:42.000 --> 00:26:52.000
should be able to produce similar results using another bank's data. Okay, so that's called replicability

00:26:52.000 --> 00:27:05.000
Transparency and ethics that usually apply to the research that involves human participants. So it requires researchers

00:27:05.000 --> 00:27:15.000
to adhere to ethical standards and also ensure informed consent and confidentiality of the

00:27:15.000 --> 00:27:20.000
Human participants' data

00:27:20.000 --> 00:27:37.000
Then the generalizability means that findings from a specific study can be applied to a larger population, different settings, or other times beyond the original group of participants

00:27:37.000 --> 00:27:43.000
So it shows if the results hold true in the real world.

00:27:43.000 --> 00:27:47.000
Then critical and logical thinking

00:27:47.000 --> 00:27:53.000
So that means that every step of a study follows valid

00:27:53.000 --> 00:28:00.000
sound rules of reasoning and involves strict

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:10.000
Useful evaluation of evidence rather than relying on guesswork, bias, or personal opinions

00:28:10.000 --> 00:28:16.000
Then, I think another feature of the research is that it must be unique, novel

00:28:16.000 --> 00:28:19.000
And have a great impact.

00:28:19.000 --> 00:28:32.000
So contribution to knowledge is one of the impact of the research. So it means that research will advance understanding challenge theories, or propose new ideas.

